<title>HONG KONG: CDL Hotels mulls hotel spinoff in HK.</title>
<headline>CDL Hotels mulls hotel spinoff in HK.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>CDL Hotels International Ltd said on Monday it is considering spinning off its hotel interests in Hong Kong, China and Taiwan on the Hong Kong stock exchange but that no formal decision has been made.</p>
<p>&quot;No formal decision has yet been made on the proposed spinoff which may or may not proceed,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;No formal application has been made to the stock exchange and no professional advisors have been engaged at this stage to advise on this issue,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>Last month, CDL led a consortium to buy a majority stake in the five-star Marriott Hotel in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>CDL shares rose HK$0.075 to HK$4.10 in early trade.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
